{
  "case_id": "2005-04-1186",
  "document_hash": "eddda0a33d9293fd806894b1c245bcba67f17f8886f397c4a851230c4cf33365",
  "records": [
    {
      "attribution": "Andrew L. Frey",
      "case_id": "2005-04-1186",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "eddda0a33d9293fd806894b1c245bcba67f17f8886f397c4a851230c4cf33365",
      "evidence_id": "ev-eddda0a33d92-0000-0002",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 6,
        "start": 6
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Both we and the Government have given Ford Motor Company as an example in the brief. If you ask somebody where is Ford Motor Company located, I venture to say that most people would say Michigan. But when you stop and think about it, it's possible that it could be also located every place where it has manufacturing facilities or sales outlets."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Kennedy",
      "case_id": "2005-04-1186",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "eddda0a33d9293fd806894b1c245bcba67f17f8886f397c4a851230c4cf33365",
      "evidence_id": "ev-eddda0a33d92-0000-0003",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 9,
        "start": 9
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE KENNEDY: Well, what would -- what would be your view? I know the question is not before us, but suppose we had a question like the principal place of business."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Andrew L. Frey",
      "case_id": "2005-04-1186",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "eddda0a33d9293fd806894b1c245bcba67f17f8886f397c4a851230c4cf33365",
      "evidence_id": "ev-eddda0a33d92-0000-0004",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 12,
        "start": 12
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "And one of the problems with the Fourth Circuit's reading is that it injects substantial ambiguity into the question of where a bank is located. It's -- the Fourth Circuit said branches, but what about where it has an office that's not a branch? What about where it stores -- where it has warehouses that store its records? What about where it has employees?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice O'Connor",
      "case_id": "2005-04-1186",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "eddda0a33d9293fd806894b1c245bcba67f17f8886f397c4a851230c4cf33365",
      "evidence_id": "ev-eddda0a33d92-0000-0005",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 13,
        "start": 13
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE O'CONNOR: Or an ATM."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "United States (Amicus Curiae)",
      "case_id": "2005-04-1186",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "eddda0a33d9293fd806894b1c245bcba67f17f8886f397c4a851230c4cf33365",
      "evidence_id": "ev-eddda0a33d92-0001-0000",
      "kind": "amicus_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 20,
        "start": 20
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "For purposes of determining its State citizenship under 28 U.S.C. 1348, a national banking association is located in the State in which its main office is found, not every State in which it may maintain a branch office or other form of physical presence."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Ginsburg",
      "case_id": "2005-04-1186",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "eddda0a33d9293fd806894b1c245bcba67f17f8886f397c4a851230c4cf33365",
      "evidence_id": "ev-eddda0a33d92-0001-0002",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 20,
        "start": 20
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE GINSBURG: What about its principal place of business if it's different from its main office?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "United States (Amicus Curiae)",
      "case_id": "2005-04-1186",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "eddda0a33d9293fd806894b1c245bcba67f17f8886f397c4a851230c4cf33365",
      "evidence_id": "ev-eddda0a33d92-0001-0001",
      "kind": "amicus_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 21,
        "start": 21
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "national banking association is a citizen of a State in which its principal place of business is found, insofar as that might be different from the State in which its main office is located."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Scalia",
      "case_id": "2005-04-1186",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "eddda0a33d9293fd806894b1c245bcba67f17f8886f397c4a851230c4cf33365",
      "evidence_id": "ev-eddda0a33d92-0001-0003",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 21,
        "start": 21
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE SCALIA: What did the Government argue in Bougas? I -- I didn't look up the briefs in the case. Did the Government appear in -- in that case?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Stevens",
      "case_id": "2005-04-1186",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "eddda0a33d9293fd806894b1c245bcba67f17f8886f397c4a851230c4cf33365",
      "evidence_id": "ev-eddda0a33d92-0001-0004",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 26,
        "start": 26
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE STEVENS: If a national bank changes its main office, it must get the approval of the Comptroller to do so?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "James R. Gilreath (Respondent)",
      "case_id": "2005-04-1186",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "eddda0a33d9293fd806894b1c245bcba67f17f8886f397c4a851230c4cf33365",
      "evidence_id": "ev-eddda0a33d92-0001-0006",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 34,
        "start": 34
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "When Congress enacts a statute that says you are deemed to be a citizen of a State -- let me be sure I read it right here -- deemed to be a citizen of the State in which you're respectively located, I don't know how Congress can speak much clearer."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Stevens",
      "case_id": "2005-04-1186",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "eddda0a33d9293fd806894b1c245bcba67f17f8886f397c4a851230c4cf33365",
      "evidence_id": "ev-eddda0a33d92-0002-0000",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 38,
        "start": 38
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE STEVENS: May I ask you -- call your attention to another word in the statute that seems persuasive to me? It's the word respectively. The statute says all national banking associations shall be, for the purposes of all other actions by or against them, be deemed citizens of the State in which they are respectively located, which I would read as saying in which each of them is located. Isn't that --"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Scalia",
      "case_id": "2005-04-1186",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "eddda0a33d9293fd806894b1c245bcba67f17f8886f397c4a851230c4cf33365",
      "evidence_id": "ev-eddda0a33d92-0002-0005",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 42,
        "start": 42
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE SCALIA: This is not a matter of -- of -- over which the Comptroller has administrative responsibility, is it?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "ABA (amicus)",
      "case_id": "2005-04-1186",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "eddda0a33d9293fd806894b1c245bcba67f17f8886f397c4a851230c4cf33365",
      "evidence_id": "ev-eddda0a33d92-0002-0003",
      "kind": "amicus_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 45,
        "start": 45
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "according to the brief by, I think, the ABA or one of the amicus, they've got something like 3,600 branches."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Court",
      "case_id": "2005-04-1186",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "eddda0a33d9293fd806894b1c245bcba67f17f8886f397c4a851230c4cf33365",
      "evidence_id": "ev-eddda0a33d92-0002-0004",
      "kind": "procedural_event",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 54,
        "start": 54
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "The case is submitted."
    }
  ],
  "schema_version": "1.0.0"
}
